#### A.1 Preliminaries

Let \(\mathbb{R}^+\) denote the positive real numbers. For a set \(S\), \(|S|\) is its cardinality. The indicator function \(\mathbf{1}_{\{condition\}}\) equals \(1\) when the condition holds and \(0\) otherwise. A tuple \(\langle a_1,\dots,a_n\rangle\) is an ordered collection.

